WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:14.708
Long ago all the beasts and birds lived together in a forest.

2
00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.289
They usually got along.

3
00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.092
But one morning, an argument erupted.

4
00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:25.374
"Birds are the greatest animals," a robin bragged.

5
00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:29.156
"We have lovely feathers and powerful wings."

6
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.581
A bear scowled.

7
00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:36.344
"Beasts have warm fur and sharp teeth."

8
00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.005
"That's right!"

9
00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.545
a fox snapped.

10
00:00:40.386 --> 00:00:43.608
All at once the birds began flapping and squawking.

11
00:00:43.628 --> 00:00:46.409
The beasts roared and stomped.

12
00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.512
A bat family sat in a tree, listening to the terrible argument.

13
00:00:51.532 --> 00:00:53.493
"Whose side should we take?"

14
00:00:53.954 --> 00:00:55.094
the mother bat whispered.

15
00:00:55.114 --> 00:01:02.294
"We have wings like birds "And fur and teeth like beasts," the father said.

16
00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:06.317
The mother bat watched the birds soar across the sky.

17
00:01:06.337 --> 00:01:09.459
"Birds are amazing," she said.

18
00:01:10.379 --> 00:01:11.440
The father nodded.

19
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.021
"Birds are the greatest animals.

20
00:01:14.802 --> 00:01:15.882
Let's join them!"

21
00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:20.065
Each day the bats flew with the birds.

22
00:01:21.586 --> 00:01:24.688
But one day the mother bat watched the beasts below.

23
00:01:25.548 --> 00:01:28.929
"The beasts' fur is beautiful," she whispered.

24
00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.030
The father bat nodded.

25
00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.752
"And their sharp teeth make them very powerful.

26
00:01:35.392 --> 00:01:36.573
I've changed my mind.

27
00:01:37.113 --> 00:01:38.794
Beasts are the greatest animals.

28
00:01:39.594 --> 00:01:40.554
Let's join them."

29
00:01:41.675 --> 00:01:44.836
After that, the bats spent all their time with the beasts.

30
00:01:46.777 --> 00:01:49.138
One afternoon another argument erupted.

31
00:01:49.998 --> 00:01:53.880
Once again the two sides argued about who the best animals were.

32
00:01:54.812 --> 00:01:56.633
The birds flapped and squawked.

33
00:01:57.253 --> 00:01:59.293
They boasted about their feathers and wings.

34
00:02:00.354 --> 00:02:02.374
The beasts roared and stomped.

35
00:02:03.094 --> 00:02:05.095
They bragged about their fur and teeth.

36
00:02:08.356 --> 00:02:10.736
Finally an old owl sighed.

37
00:02:10.756 --> 00:02:14.917
"This argument is so silly.

38
00:02:14.937 --> 00:02:16.858
We must meet with the beasts.

39
00:02:17.538 --> 00:02:19.539
Surely we can have peace in the forest again."

40
00:02:21.399 --> 00:02:23.920
And so the birds and the beasts held a meeting.

41
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.841
Everyone agreed it was time to return peace to the forest.

42
00:02:28.441 --> 00:02:30.862
The birds and the beasts held a celebration.

43
00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:35.583
The bats flew over, ready to join everyone.

44
00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:39.824
But to their surprise, the others looked angry.

45
00:02:40.644 --> 00:02:42.325
The old owl blinked at them.

46
00:02:42.345 --> 00:02:46.066
"You joined the beasts when you thought they were the greatest animals.

47
00:02:46.946 --> 00:02:48.867
The bear growled softly.

48
00:02:48.887 --> 00:02:53.548
"And you joined the birds when you thought they were the greatest."

49
00:02:54.592 --> 00:02:57.795
"But um The bats tried to explain.

50
00:02:57.815 --> 00:03:01.318
"Hmpf!" The birds snorted and flapped away.

51
00:03:02.158 --> 00:03:03.660
The beasts turned their backs.

52
00:03:08.484 --> 00:03:09.845
The mother bat hung her head.

53
00:03:09.865 --> 00:03:12.867
"We joined each side when it suited us."

54
00:03:13.948 --> 00:03:15.389
The father nodded sadly.

55
00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:18.672
"We should have stayed loyal to one side."

56
00:03:19.773 --> 00:03:22.776
The bats flew off to a cave, far from the others.

57
00:03:23.645 --> 00:03:28.817
Ever since then, bats hide in dark caves, flying only at night.
